-# Checkpoint 7
-Change: Tried calendar features (purchase month, day of month, promised-date weekday); reverted from FEATS.
-Why: Seasonal peaks and holidays may raise late rates.
-Validation PR-AUC: 0.2171 -> 0.1779 (reverted state: 0.2171)
-Decision: reverted, PR-AUC dropped 0.039. Training covers each calendar month once or twice, so month/day-of-month mostly memorize specific past events and don't generalize to a later period.
+# Checkpoint 8
+Change: Regularized LightGBM (300 trees, lr 0.02, 15 leaves, min_child_samples 100, subsampling, L2 5) instead of defaults.
+Why: Default settings overfit a small, noisy target (about 7% positives); stronger regularization generalizes better to a later period.
+Validation PR-AUC: 0.2171 -> 0.2318
+Decision: kept, PR-AUC improved by 0.0147 (ROC-AUC 0.6701 -> 0.6816, Brier 0.1050 -> 0.1044). Hand-picked, not searched.
